      "writtenOn": "2026-06-10T18:50:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it possible that after zram_writeback_slots() is done, confirmed that wb_ctl-\u003enum_inflight is 0 and called release_wb_ctl() the task is preempted and some other task calls zram_writeback_slots(), which calls zram_writeback_endio(), which adds an entry into wb_ctl-\u003edone_reqs? If so, then there is a possibility that release_wb_ctl() will later be called while wb_ctl-\u003edone_reqs is not empty. What prevents this scenario?",
      "parentUuid": "9c591980_6d04b256",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 835,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 835,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "d2b2a06b31dd585472c91e1d4496f0a4fb2adbc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21d8ba8b_9ada9910",
        "filename": "drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 835,
      "author": {
        "id": 1894539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-11T03:17:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, that scenario cannot happen. It is prevented by two independent mechanisms in zram: per-invocation wb_ctl allocation and device-level mutual exclusion via pp_in_progress.\n\n1. wb_ctl is allocated per-writeback invocation (Not shared)\n`wb_ctl \u003d init_wb_ctl(zram);`\n2. Writeback concurrency is strictly mutually excluded.\nzram-\u003epp_in_progress is reset back to 0 only after release_wb_ctl() has fully finished.",
      "parentUuid": "7d5da82a_fe7bca98",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 835,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 835,
        "endChar": 10
      },
